==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|lāzzen|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|lāzzan|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*lētaną}}. Akin to Dutch {{term|laten|lang=nl}}, English {{term|let|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈlasn̩]|[ˈlasən]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-lassen.ogg|audio (Germany)}}
* {{audio|De-at-lassen.ogg|audio (Austria)}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=7|lässt|ließ|gelassen|past participle 2=lassen|past subjunctive=ließe}}

# {{context|auxiliary|with an infinitive|past participle: “[[lassen]]”|lang=de}} to [[allow]]; to [[permit]]; to [[let]]
# {{context|auxiliary|with an infinitive|past participle: “[[lassen]]”|lang=de}} to [[have]] someone (do something); to have (something done); to [[make]] (something happen); to [[cause]] (something to be done)
#: ''etwas machen '''lassen''''' — “to have something done”
#: ''jemanden etwas tun '''lassen''''' — “to have someone do something”
# {{context|transitive|past participle: “[[gelassen]]”|lang=de}} to [[let]]; to [[leave]]
# {{context|transitive|past participle: “[[gelassen]]”|lang=de}} to [[stop]] (something); to [[quit]]; to [[refrain]] from; to [[help]] doing (something)
# {{context|intransitive|past participle: “[[gelassen]]”|lang=de}} to [[cease]]; to [[desist]]

====Usage notes====
Note that the English phrases "to ''let'' someone do something" and "to ''make'' someone do something" both translate into German as ''jemanden etwas tun lassen''. In order to avoid ambiguity, "to let" can be expressed as ''jemandem [[erlauben]], etwas zu tun'', and "to make" can be expressed as ''jemanden dazu [[bringen]], etwas zu tun''.

